                    {
                        "form_id": "33124d6e-b0c1-4e53-a53c-86a1fb100dba",
                        "entry_id": "884ebf85-3d86-3233-9b76-7aa32b2111fe",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "крючкотво́рствах"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "43af6ac7-1aaa-331e-b947-cf86818cf7b6",
                        "entry_id": "884ebf85-3d86-3233-9b76-7aa32b2111fe",
                        "glosses": [
                            "разг. преднамеренное нагромождение формальностей, мелочей и использование их в корыстных целях, канцелярская волокита, бюрократические придирки"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fe10dd9e-c241-44c5-a4f1-098e282cacf1",
                                "sense_id": "43af6ac7-1aaa-331e-b947-cf86818cf7b6",
                                "text": "Тут нет ни крючкотворства с насилием и взяточничеством, ни грязных плутов, ни официальных злодеев, объясняющих изящным языком, что они — благодетели общества, ни мещан, мужиков и маленьких чиновников, мучимых всеми этими ужасными и гадкими людьми."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0e24ed47-e7fc-4309-9a3b-988c8f86db6b",
                                "sense_id": "43af6ac7-1aaa-331e-b947-cf86818cf7b6",
                                "text": "Его встречают одними циническими насмешками, подозрительностью и крючкотворством из-за спорных денег; он слышит лишь разговоры и житейские правила, от которых воротит сердце, ежедневно „за коньячком“, и, наконец, зрит отца, отбивающего у него, у сына, на его же сыновние деньги, любовницу, — о господа присяжные, это отвратительно и жестоко!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c846da23-4d67-437a-ad64-9ba7de09b1bb",
                                "sense_id": "43af6ac7-1aaa-331e-b947-cf86818cf7b6",
                                "text": "Эти лубочные листы, может быть, наивно, но искренно и выразительно высмеивали жадность и грубость дворянства, лихоимство чиновничества, крючкотворство и продажность судебных властей."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d72cf881-743e-406f-ade2-a823436e47da",
                        "source_entry_id": "884ebf85-3d86-3233-9b76-7aa32b2111fe",
                        "source_sense_id": "43af6ac7-1aaa-331e-b947-cf86818cf7b6",
                        "target_lang_word": "chicane",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "chicane",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "056fa917-ed87-3bd3-8d6a-24bc7c73f48a",
                                        "entry_id": "6eff4b3a-b92a-386b-ba4d-1c86ba14b58a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A quibble, a pedantic or dishonest objection; an act of deception."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1547bdaf-2121-36db-b8e3-f76913eefda2",
                                        "entry_id": "6eff4b3a-b92a-386b-ba4d-1c86ba14b58a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The use of dishonest means or subterfuge to achieve one's (especially political) goals; chicanery, trickery."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f15b514f-d81a-4ccf-a828-2bb18af290ef",
                                                "sense_id": "1547bdaf-2121-36db-b8e3-f76913eefda2",
                                                "text": "1775, Edmund Burke, speech on conciliation with America\nIn this character of the Americans, a love of freedom is the predominating feature which marks and distinguishes the whole; and as an ardent is always a jealous affection, your Colonies become suspicious, restive, and untractable whenever they see the least attempt to wrest from them by force, or shuffle from them by chicane, what they think the only advantage worth living for."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "04b60d72-3566-41b6-9d7c-8a443908104b",
                                                "sense_id": "1547bdaf-2121-36db-b8e3-f76913eefda2",
                                                "text": "‘That they may be unlearned in the detestable chicane of politics, is certain; but, they are also uncorrupted by the odious and pernicious maxims of the unfeeling tools of despotism.’"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e44109b8-e1cf-3edd-a70f-e16f6501462a",
                                        "entry_id": "6eff4b3a-b92a-386b-ba4d-1c86ba14b58a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The holding of a hand without trumps, or the hand itself."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c0c030fb-d383-3b4b-9e25-3dbeaa35a898",
                                        "entry_id": "6eff4b3a-b92a-386b-ba4d-1c86ba14b58a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A sharp double bend on a racecourse, designed to prevent unsafe speeds; an obstacle creating a curve."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e8be5e51-e0f5-4eb8-98ca-bfab39a2ecca",
                                                "sense_id": "c0c030fb-d383-3b4b-9e25-3dbeaa35a898",
                                                "text": "On lap 23, Hamilton got a run on Leclerc into the second chicane after the two had overtaken Nico Hulkenberg's out-of-stop-sequence Renault down the main straight."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "55e09a17-6733-3ffa-861d-48f946eb2098",
                                        "entry_id": "6eff4b3a-b92a-386b-ba4d-1c86ba14b58a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A raised area or other obstacle around which vehicles must drive, especially designed to reduce speed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "chicane",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "77b146e5-5f8e-3755-ac88-94275759c332",
                                        "entry_id": "9b709034-6a27-3c1f-b0d6-1752fc83ea05",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To use chicanery, tricks, or subterfuge."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ae94ba86-b3fb-3f2b-a890-7194e8524d37",
                                        "entry_id": "9b709034-6a27-3c1f-b0d6-1752fc83ea05",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To deceive."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
