                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "eaf24f92-1fc8-4332-b577-184cd24bfc81",
                        "source_entry_id": "884ebf85-3d86-3233-9b76-7aa32b2111fe",
                        "source_sense_id": "43af6ac7-1aaa-331e-b947-cf86818cf7b6",
                        "target_lang_word": "chicanery",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "chicanery",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fd5b8fbf-ca1e-3575-b9cc-75e906b9666c",
                                        "entry_id": "7b1ef6b8-87de-39be-96db-4165babae7ff",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Deception by the use of trickery, quibbling, or subterfuge."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ef0282c9-dbf5-4694-9e2d-b100e1a37f31",
                                                "sense_id": "fd5b8fbf-ca1e-3575-b9cc-75e906b9666c",
                                                "text": "They do not always find manors, got by rapine or chicanery, insensibly to melt away, as the poets will have it; or that all gold glides, like thawing snow, from the thief’s hand that grasps it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6177b9ee-2ee4-4bf7-a067-b04cb9fd505c",
                                                "sense_id": "fd5b8fbf-ca1e-3575-b9cc-75e906b9666c",
                                                "text": "He covered his tracks, he got that idiot at the copy shop to lie for him. You think this is something? You think this is bad? This? This chicanery? He's done worse. That billboard! Are you telling me that a man just happens to fall like that? No! He orchestrated it! Jimmy!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a259b720-5ed0-439c-96cb-ab68eb521680",
                                                "sense_id": "fd5b8fbf-ca1e-3575-b9cc-75e906b9666c",
                                                "text": "Having survived “The Long Night,” Daenerys will now be turning her attention back to the problem that originally vexed her: Cersei Lannister. It will be interesting to see how the show tries to raise the stakes of an internecine squabble between competing monarchs when compared to an existential threat to humanity’s very existence, but this series has always excelled when it goes deep on the machinations of political chicanery."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "118cbf6d-67c0-370e-bf14-ce18c3b6e70c",
                                        "entry_id": "7b1ef6b8-87de-39be-96db-4165babae7ff",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An individual act of trickery or deception."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d91915ef-91b2-4320-897d-e774d48f2133",
                                                "sense_id": "118cbf6d-67c0-370e-bf14-ce18c3b6e70c",
                                                "text": "Stanford University's honor code dates to 1921, written by students to help guide them through the minefield of plagiarism, forbidden collaboration, copying and other chicaneries that have tempted undergraduates since they first arrived on college campuses."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e448561d-e37a-3a0a-86fd-a568825bf429",
                                        "entry_id": "7b1ef6b8-87de-39be-96db-4165babae7ff",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The quality of being inclined to trickery or deceitfulness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cb8a4962-b571-4151-8b91-deef6ad5a135",
                                                "sense_id": "e448561d-e37a-3a0a-86fd-a568825bf429",
                                                "text": "He carried home with him all the knaviſh chicanery of the loweſt pettifogger, together with a wife whom he had purchſed of a drayman for twenty pounds; and he ſoon found means to obtain a Dedimus as an acting juſtice of peace."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b772b87d-1bdf-4968-a8f7-7cf043521df8",
                        "source_entry_id": "884ebf85-3d86-3233-9b76-7aa32b2111fe",
                        "source_sense_id": "43af6ac7-1aaa-331e-b947-cf86818cf7b6",
                        "target_lang_word": "pettifoggery",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "pettifoggery",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7d87944f-6ea8-3a05-8a6b-6286cbb5a5e9",
                                        "entry_id": "ba8e5d8c-a4de-35b6-abbc-b8381c567b46",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The actions of a pettifogger; a trivial quarrel."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "92c3a080-4dba-4975-aca6-96c6e9d2ce88",
                                                "sense_id": "7d87944f-6ea8-3a05-8a6b-6286cbb5a5e9",
                                                "text": "He was capable of using lawyerly rhetoric, at times, to the brink of pettifoggery."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d5d30081-5b92-4da3-a61c-4389e6a389bc",
                                                "sense_id": "7d87944f-6ea8-3a05-8a6b-6286cbb5a5e9",
                                                "text": "Yet even Harlan was to prove capable of grievous pettifoggery on the racial issue."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "375c3309-fc33-47ac-bfc3-8ce1aee6e6db",
                                                "sense_id": "7d87944f-6ea8-3a05-8a6b-6286cbb5a5e9",
                                                "text": "[Frankfurter's reasoning in Beauharnais v. Illinois] struck Black and the other three Roosevelt appointees who joined his dissent as noxious pettifoggery[.]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1065c5ab-5473-419b-8945-2be3645de907",
                                                "sense_id": "7d87944f-6ea8-3a05-8a6b-6286cbb5a5e9",
                                                "text": "The idea that a minor bureaucratic restructuring could have made any difference in the time of Trump reflected how immune bureaucratic pettifoggery is to reality."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8c931c07-2cb3-489a-8d3c-b14278e8a8fa",
                        "source_entry_id": "884ebf85-3d86-3233-9b76-7aa32b2111fe",
                        "source_sense_id": "43af6ac7-1aaa-331e-b947-cf86818cf7b6",
                        "target_lang_word": "Rechtsverdrehung",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ffef195c-05ac-408e-9ad3-fe5a432c4ba9",
                        "source_entry_id": "884ebf85-3d86-3233-9b76-7aa32b2111fe",
                        "source_sense_id": "43af6ac7-1aaa-331e-b947-cf86818cf7b6",
                        "target_lang_word": "Schikane",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Schikane",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "26b9fa37-065e-3e92-bc78-a3773592c27d",
                                        "entry_id": "3dab0f14-532d-33e0-be51-3edf8353937a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "eine absichtlich gestellte Schwierigkeit, um irgendjemandem etwas zu erschweren; eine hämische Plackerei"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "49e61576-6047-45ae-9c43-174fb2a05f11",
                                                "sense_id": "26b9fa37-065e-3e92-bc78-a3773592c27d",
                                                "text": "An seinem Arbeitsplatz musste er viele Schikanen erdulden."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e9cc8063-d33d-47d1-a23c-0a06a49fa4e2",
                                                "sense_id": "26b9fa37-065e-3e92-bc78-a3773592c27d",
                                                "text": "„Aber es darf keine Schikane werden.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "76123d87-5d57-4b7e-9e40-db52dfb0c54d",
                                                "sense_id": "26b9fa37-065e-3e92-bc78-a3773592c27d",
                                                "text": "„Und sobald er weinte, weil er sich ja nicht wehren durfte, begann die Schikane von neuem.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fdef7e27-0e77-4efb-8814-ffa907024af9",
                                                "sense_id": "26b9fa37-065e-3e92-bc78-a3773592c27d",
                                                "text": "„Zwei oder drei Mal griff er noch ein, dann hörten die Hänseleien und Schikanen der anderen Kinder auf.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aa47600b-1bef-408f-85a7-0f4fab259cb4",
                                                "sense_id": "26b9fa37-065e-3e92-bc78-a3773592c27d",
                                                "text": "„Trotz aller Schikanen, Frivolitäten und Lügen glaubte ich an sie.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5654b2e3-aea6-3f3e-8fc2-f5d91d3d8b54",
                                        "entry_id": "3dab0f14-532d-33e0-be51-3edf8353937a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "besonders schwieriger Streckenabschnitt"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Rennsport"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "de744391-603e-4ebb-a9f5-9049d3c35abf",
                                                "sense_id": "5654b2e3-aea6-3f3e-8fc2-f5d91d3d8b54",
                                                "text": "In der ersten Schikane verfuhr er sich und verlor dabei viel Zeit."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f58bcdd0-c237-405d-b1cf-555a42258f79",
                        "source_entry_id": "884ebf85-3d86-3233-9b76-7aa32b2111fe",
                        "source_sense_id": "43af6ac7-1aaa-331e-b947-cf86818cf7b6",
